Title: Complete API
Section: Complete API > API Reference Overview > Open Connect > Expression Interface > `duckdb_column_data` > Parameters + adjacent subsections

* `result`: The result object to fetch the column data from.

Related subsection: Complete API > API Reference Overview > Open Connect > Expression Interface > `duckdb_column_data` > Return Value

The column data of the specified column.

Related subsection: Complete API > API Reference Overview > Open Connect > Expression Interface > `duckdb_nullmask_data`

Returns the nullmask of a specific column of a result in columnar format. The nullmask indicates for every row whether or not the corresponding row is `NULL`. If a row is `NULL`, the values present in the array provided by `duckdb_column_data` are undefined.

```c
int32_t *data = (int32_t *) duckdb_column_data(&result, 0);
bool *nullmask = duckdb_nullmask_data(&result, 0);
if (nullmask[row]) {
    printf("Data for row %d: NULL\n", row);
} else {
    printf("Data for row %d: %d\n", row, data[row]);
}
```

